{
  "audio": "015.just-as-important.mp3",
  "paragraph": 15,
  "text": "Just as important as accuracy is economics, and the secret weapon publicized by teams like Manus and Claude Code is KV prompt caching. In a thirty-turn coding session, you re-send the conversation history on every single turn. If your harness keeps the system prompt and tool schemas token-identical at the prefix and appends new turns strictly to the end, the model provider reuses cached attention states from previous turns. That slashes input token costs and cuts time to first token dramatically across long agent loops.",
